wm(a,b){return a+" found no evidence this time, so it did not take part in the vote (role weight "+b+"%). This means it spotted no AI traces on its own axis \u2014 not that it considers the text human-written."},
wl(a,b){return a+" found only a weak directional signal. It is discounted for screening and does not count as threshold-qualified evidence (role weight cap "+b+"%)."},
xu(a){return"Only "+a+" produced a usable direction; the other engines turned up nothing this time. The conclusion rests on a single analysis axis, so treat its confidence accordingly."},
xt(a){return""+a+" further engine(s) ran but formed no directional signal, and were excluded so that 'nothing to report' is not miscounted as 'looks human-written'."},
gpH(){return"Perplexity was not used for this document: the perplexity model (DistilGPT2) was trained on English only, and on Chinese, Japanese or Korean text it measures byte predictability rather than language predictability. Measured on labelled data, it separates human from AI writing in those languages 0% of the time, so counting it would only manufacture false positives."},
nR(a){return"Baseline by language: "+a},
nU(a){return""+a+" earlier sample(s) carry no language tag and cannot join any language's baseline \u2014 the original text is not kept, so the language cannot be recovered after the fact. They will be replaced as new documents are analysed."},
m5(a,b){return"Routed to \u201c"+a+"\u201d for this document: the variant you selected is not validated for "+b+", and this one is."},
m2(a,b){return"\u201c"+a+"\u201d is a multilingual model but has not been validated on "+b+", so treat its score as weaker evidence than a validated one."},
m3(a,b){return"\u201c"+a+"\u201d does not cover "+b+". Its score is shown for reference only and should not be read as evidence either way."},
gpD(){return"Perplexity was not used: the language of this document could not be determined, so there is no calibrated threshold to compare against. Guessing a language would mean applying the wrong scale \u2014 the mistake this check exists to prevent."},
pG(a,b){return"Perplexity was not used: the model in use (\u201c"+a+"\u201d) has no measured threshold for "+b+" yet. Its raw value carries no meaning without a calibrated scale, so it is left out rather than guessed at."},
gte(){return"This format carries no editing record. PDFs, images and pasted text hold no history of how they were written, so the analysis rests entirely on text statistics. If you can obtain the original .docx, .odt or .doc, its editing history is far stronger evidence \u2014 and unlike text statistics, it does not weaken as language models improve."},
gwI(){return"A low score is not confirmation that a person wrote this. With no origin evidence available, this verdict rests only on text statistics, which reliably flag formulaic writing but not well-written output from current-generation models."},
gwP(){return"The file's own editing record contradicts this low score. Origin evidence does not weaken as language models improve, whereas text statistics cannot identify well-written output from current-generation models. Read the origin evidence below before drawing any conclusion from the score above."},
vI(a,b,c){return""+a+" of "+b+" paragraphs share a single editing batch and carry "+c+"% of the words \u2014 consistent with that block being written or pasted in one sitting, even though the file has other editing batches."},
qg(a){return""+a+" character-level evasion marks were found (zero-width characters, look-alike letters, or direction controls). Ordinary writing tools do not produce these \u2014 someone processed the text to defeat detection."},
qe(a,b){return""+a+" of "+b+" cited works could not be found in any of the reference databases checked. Fabricated citations are a behaviour of language models, and unlike writing style, whether a paper exists is a verifiable fact."},
qd(a){return"All "+a+" cited works were located in public reference databases."},
qf(a,b){return"The file records "+a+" minutes of editing across "+b+" saves, which is consistent with the text having been written in this document."},
qi(a,b){return"Source DOI "+a+" matches this document and was registered in "+b+", before modern generative-AI writing systems."},
qh(a){return"Source DOI "+a+" resolves, but its registered title does not match this document. Verify the document identity before relying on it."},
gmU(){return"Segment stability unavailable \xb7 no sentence-level evidence voted"},
gtk(){return"No authorship-specific evidence strong enough for escalation was found. The result shown is the best directional screening available, not a claim that AI and human evidence are evenly split."},
gxg(){return"What can be verified"},
gxf(){return"Each item below can be checked independently. Unlike a probability, these do not weaken as language models improve."},
qk(a,b){return"The text was typed in this app over "+a+" minutes, with "+b+" characters revised along the way. Writing that happens here leaves a record no language model can reproduce."},
gmc(){return"Multi-evidence assessment"},
gmb(){return"Six axes are shown separately. Only authorship-specific evidence affects the author verdict; coverage shows what could be examined."},
